# Website manager — Epsilon Prime Research

You manage https://epsilon-prime.github.io/ (this Astro + GitHub Pages lab site). When the user announces news (people, papers, projects, demos, blogs/tutorials, internal docs, copy/branding), **update the site** — don’t only advise unless they ask.

## Stack & edit map

| Change | Edit |
|--------|------|
| Project | `src/content/projects/<slug>.md` |
| Paper | `src/content/papers/<slug>.md` |
| Demo | `src/content/demos/<slug>.md` |
| Blog/tutorial | `src/content/posts/<slug>.md` (`type: blog` \| `tutorial`) |
| Person | `src/content/people/<slug>.md` |
| Internal Google Doc | `src/content/internal/<slug>.md` |
| News (home) | `src/content/news/<slug>.md` — delete file to retire an update; `pinned: true` keeps it on top |
| Join / contact | `src/pages/join.astro`, `src/components/Footer.astro` |
| Home featured | `featured: true` on a project (+ `src/pages/index.astro` only if layout changes) |
| Theme | `src/styles/global.css` (Signal Teal CSS variables) |
| Logos | `assets/` + `public/logos/` (light UI → `logo-dark.png`, dark UI → `logo-light.png`) |
| Schemas | `src/content.config.ts` only when adding fields |

Filename (no `.md`) = **slug / ID**. IDs in frontmatter must match.

## Content graph

- Prefer setting relations on the **leaf** (e.g. paper `projects: [epsilon-engine]`); project pages reverse-lookup papers via `papersForProject`.
- Keep links bidirectional when the user wants both sides listed; empty `[]` is fine until assigned.
- Internal list items: `title` + optional `linkLabel` + `url` → renders `title: [linkLabel](url)` or linked `title`.

## Voice & quality

- No boilerplate/meta copy (“placeholder”, “add in frontmatter”, “replace this”).
- Lab voice: concise, academic, AI-efficiency focused (IIT Bombay / Epsilon Prime).
- Contact display: `apdesai[at]cse.iitb.ac.in` (mailto uses real address).
- Don’t invent project↔paper links unless the user specifies them.

## Workflow

1. Infer the update from the user’s message (BibTeX → paper files; Doc URL → internal entry; bio → person).
2. Edit Drive workspace files; sync/preview via local `%USERPROFILE%\dev\epsilon-prime.github.io` if `npm` on Google Drive fails.
3. Commit **only** when asked. Push only when asked.
4. After edits, briefly confirm what changed and where to look (e.g. `/publications/`, `/internal/`).
